	(text "U1 pin numbers are the SuperMini's pads, seen from its\ncomponent side with USB-C at the top: pads 1-8 run DOWN\nthe left edge, pads 9-16 run UP the right edge (counted\nlike a DIP chip). Pad 1 = GPIO5 (the square pad on the\nPCB), pad 16 = 5V. It is soldered to the BACK of the PCB,\ncomponents facing away from the board, USB-C at the\nboard's right-hand edge."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 111.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b4b87158-117d-5b08-89c7-7369b9401366")
	)
	(text "U2, U3 (DIP-16): hold the chip with the notch at the top. Pin 1 is top-left, next to the notch\n(often also marked with a dot). Count DOWN the left side 1-8, then UP the right side 9-16."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.84 109.22 0)
